From a64891d36ca5e2eb08a1e294110fffe365e326f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 20:07:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02929/11362] [outer-loop] variant-augmentation bridge for the
 cross-game verifier (reflection, v2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements + validates the operator-requested variant augmentation of the verifier
training corpus. collect_pooled(variants=K) replays each banked solve once and featurizes
under identity + K reflections (horizontal/vertical), yielding K+1x labeled
(frame -> steps-to-go) training points with known-correct labels on reflected layouts.

HONEST finding (validated, drove the design): color-permutation AND the v1 5-scalar features
are augmentation-INVARIANT (color-agnostic + symmetric by design) -> recolor variants are exact
duplicates (weights unchanged). Only REFLECTION + the v2 occupancy map adds real signal
(|Δ|≈0.23/frame); main() auto-selects v2 when variants>0. Validated: v2 baseline weight 214.6
-> augmented 42.0, i.e. reflection regularizes an overfit position-specific weight toward the
reflection-invariance the held-out eval games reward. 4 regression tests pin the v1-invariant /
v2-diversified distinction + the label semantics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
